CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ unqualified typedef read: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ qualified typedef read: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ decltype typedef read: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ member template decltype typedef read: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
In-class static data member initializers reading class-local typedefs
(unqualified, qualified, and via decltype over declared-only member
functions/member function templates) -- N5008 [basic.scope.class].  Distilled from the __is_swappable probe shape
(cpp11_is_swappable_unevaluated): cbmc used to swallow the mid-elaboration
resolution failure and leave the member's value as a raw cpp_name that read
as nondet.  Fixed by queueing cpp_name-bearing initializers and
re-type-checking them in the class scope at the end of the class.
g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
